<title>CHINA: China to choose dam project generators on Aug 15.</title>
<headline>China to choose dam project generators on Aug 15.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>China will on August 15 choose a winner from six tenders submitted by international consortia competing to supply generators for the huge Three Gorges dam project, an official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China has said the groups in the running include Siemens AG and GE Canada; Anglo-French group GEC Alsthom; Swedish-Swiss ABB, ABB a Russian consortium; a Japanese group; and Impsa of Argentina as well as Westinghouse of Canada.</p>
<p>The official of the Beijing representative office of the China Yangtze Three Gorges Project Development Corp declined to give any further details of the companies involved or of the bidding process.</p>
<p>Officials in April said the winning tender would be decided by late June or early July and have given no explanation for the apparent delay.</p>
<p>The Three Gorges project will require at least 14 generating units with a total installed capacity of 9,800 megawatts, state media have said. The huge project, which aims to tame the mighty Yangtze River, is scheduled for completion in 2009.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
